<section class="policy-content">
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p>
    At <strong>The Sports Scoop</strong> (accessible at <a href="https://www.thesportsscoop.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">www.thesportsscoop.com</a>), we take your privacy seriously. This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, and safeguard your information when you visit our website.
  </p>

  <p>
    If you have any questions or concerns about our policy, please contact us at support@thesportsscoop.com.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Consent</h2>
  <p>By using our website, you consent to our Privacy Policy and agree to its terms.</p>

  <h2>2. Information We Collect</h2>
  <p>We collect information that you voluntarily provide to us, such as your name, email address, or phone number when you contact us or subscribe to updates.</p>
  <p>We may also collect information when you register for an account, such as your address, company name, or preferences.</p>

  <h2>3. How We Use Your Information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To operate and maintain the website</li>
    <li>To improve user experience and personalize content</li>
    <li>To communicate with you for support, updates, and marketing</li>
    <li>To analyze website usage and trends</li>
    <li>To prevent fraud and enhance security</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Log Files</h2>
  <p>
    Like many websites, The Sports Scoop uses log files. These files log visitors when they access our site. This may include your IP address, browser type, ISP, date/time stamp, referring pages, and other data used to analyze trends and administer the site.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Cookies and Web Beacons</h2>
  <p>
    We use cookies to store user preferences and session data to optimize your experience. These cookies help personalize content and track visitor behavior.
  </p>

  <h3>Google DoubleClick DART Cookie</h3>
  <p>
    Google, as a third-party vendor, uses DART cookies to serve ads based on your visit to our site and others. You may opt out by visiting Google’s Ad Policy page: 
    <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads" target="_blank" rel="noopener">https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Advertising Partners</h2>
  <p>
    Some advertisers on our site may use cookies and web beacons. These third-party ad servers automatically receive your IP address when this occurs. Their privacy practices are governed by their own policies.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Third-Party Privacy Policies</h2>
  <p>
    Our Privacy Policy does not apply to other websites or advertisers. Please consult their policies for detailed information on their practices and how to opt out of certain services.
  </p>

  <h2>8. CCPA Privacy Rights</h2>
  <p>Under the California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA), you have the right to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Request disclosure of the categories and specific personal data we collect</li>
    <li>Request deletion of your personal data</li>
    <li>Opt-out of the sale of your personal data</li>
  </ul>
  <p>If you make a request, we will respond within one month. To exercise any of these rights, please email us at support@thesportsscoop.com.</p>

  <h2>9. GDPR Data Protection Rights</h2>
  <p>If you are a resident of the European Economic Area (EEA), you have the right to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Access your personal data</li>
    <li>Request correction or erasure of your data</li>
    <li>Object to or restrict our processing of your data</li>
    <li>Data portability</li>
  </ul>
  <p>To exercise these rights, please contact us at support@thesportsscoop.com.</p>

  <h2>10. Children's Information</h2>
  <p>
    Protecting children online is a priority. The Sports Scoop does not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13. If you believe your child provided such data, please contact us immediately so we can remove it.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Changes to This Policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this Privacy Policy occasionally. Changes will be posted on this page with a revised "Last updated" date.
  </p>
  <p>Last updated: June 3, 2025</p>
</section>

